"""make-eval-set: build the accuracy eval set eval/dev-v1 for `hark eval run --set` (docs/eval.md).

    scripts/make-eval-set                     # eval/dev-v1 (downloads cached in models/eval-cache)
    scripts/make-eval-set --out DIR --only syn-007 --only real-003

Two parts, each clip a directory with audio.wav (16 kHz mono PCM16), context.json (the key-down
snapshot exactly as `retry.save` writes it) and label.json (said / critical / forbidden /
accepted / note):

- syn-NNN: the developer prompts in scripts/eval_prompts.py, synthesized with Kokoro-82M
  (kokoro-onnx, Apache-2.0) and macOS `say` across en_US/GB/AU/IE/IN/ZA and non-native voices,
  rates, room reverb, a laptop-mic colour and background noise (DEMAND, CC-BY-4.0, plus
  synthetic fan and keyboard noise) at realistic SNRs. TTS reads the spoken form only.
- real-NNN: real speech from public datasets (EdACC, CC-BY-SA-4.0: conversational English in many
  accents; LibriSpeech, CC-BY-4.0: read speech), paired with a dense hark shortlist. Clips whose
  words collide with real hark identifiers ("wait for" / `wait_for`) are preferred, and those
  identifiers are put on the list and into `forbidden`: they measure false substitutions.

Everything is seeded; the same inputs give the same clips. Reviewed texts (`accepted`) in an
existing label.json are kept when its `said` is unchanged. Needs macOS (`say`, `afconvert`).
"""

